# RELAXED excited-state dipole (run gradient triggers CPSCF orbital relaxation).
# gamma_0 = angle(mu, delta_mu) is the two-photon parameter Cusick measure as 22 deg;
# ours is 44.3 deg from UNRELAXED dipoles, and delta_mu is a difference of two large
# nearly-cancelling vectors, so relaxation can matter disproportionately. This tests it.
# Basis-consistent STEOM correction, 2026-08-28.
# IDENTICAL to tddft_ensemble_decoherence/reference_pilot/reference_current.in
# (which produced the calibration value 3.43441587 eV) except basis:
#   6-311g**  ->  def2-svpd
# Same geometry (sha256 86287ad551f28029..., 44 atoms), same 2352 point charges,
# same functional, charge, multiplicity and CIS settings.
# Purpose: the existing Delta_STEOM mixes TDDFT/6-311G** with STEOM/def2-SVPD, so
# it conflates the method difference with a basis change. Matching the basis
# isolates the pure method (DFT vs STEOM-CCSD) difference.
coordinates /home/robson/PetaChem/tc_tddft_44/geometry.xyz
run gradient
cis yes
basis def2-svpd
method wb97xd3
charge -1
spinmult 1
pointcharges /home/robson/PetaChem/tc_tddft_44/mm_charges.dat
scrdir scr_relax_wb97xd3
cisnumstates 5
cistarget 2
cismaxiter 200
cismax 500
scf diis+a
threall 1.0e-13
gpus 1
end
